# _redirects — Cloudflare Pages / Netlify rewrite rules.
#
# Canonical URLs are the real .html files (see <link rel="canonical"> and
# sitemap.xml). These rules make the extensionless forms work as conveniences
# without duplicating content: /career/apply and /career/apply.html both serve
# the same page, and the canonical tag keeps search engines on the .html URL.
#
# GitHub Pages ignores this file. There, only the .html forms exist — which is
# exactly why the .html URLs are canonical. Deploy through Cloudflare Pages to
# get the pretty URLs.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- careers ---
/career                       /career/index.html          301
/career/                      /career/index.html          301
/career/login                 /career/login.html           301
/career/register              /career/register.html        301
/career/apply                 /career/apply.html           301
/career/dashboard             /career/dashboard.html       301
/career/article-assistant     /career/article-assistant.html 301

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ admin ---
# Not linked from the public site; the 301s exist so a typed /admin/... URL
# lands on the right page instead of a 404.
/admin                        /admin/index.html           301
/admin/                       /admin/index.html           301
/admin/vacancies              /admin/vacancies.html        301
/admin/applications           /admin/applications.html    301
/admin/login                  /admin/login.html            301

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- safety ---
# Markdown vacancy sources live in /careers/drafts and /careers/_published and
# are build inputs, not pages. On GitHub Pages a .md file would be served as a
# downloadable raw file, exposing the text of a vacancy before it is published.
# Block the whole /careers tree.
/careers/*                    /404                         404